---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Base title="How It Works — MetaPainting">

  <Hero
    title="How It Works"
    subtitle="A step-by-step guide to creating collaborative art that engages crowds and reveals hidden layers."
    backgroundImage="/paintings/yoga-man/progress-3.jpg"
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">

      <div class="intro reveal">
        <p class="font-serif intro__text">
          MetaPainting is a technique and a philosophy. Every piece begins with a structural design,
          invites dozens of participants to contribute, and culminates in a dramatic blacklight reveal.
          Here's how to create your own.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- STEPS -->
      <div class="steps">

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">01</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">Concept & Design</h3>
            <p>Start with a theme that resonates with your group. The design should have clear structure —
            bold outlines, defined regions — so participants know where to paint. Think of it as a
            coloring book for collaboration, but one where going outside the lines is part of the beauty.</p>
            <div class="step__tip">
              <strong>Tip:</strong> Use vector software (Illustrator, Inkscape) to create your design.
              This lets you scale to any canvas size and project outlines onto the surface.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">02</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">Materials & Setup</h3>
            <p>You'll need a large canvas or primed surface, acrylic paints in a curated palette,
            brushes of various sizes, and — the secret ingredient — UV-reactive (phosphorescent) paints
            for the blacklight layer.</p>
            <div class="step__tip">
              <strong>Tip:</strong> Set up a paint station with pre-mixed colors. Limit the palette to
              prevent muddy results. Label zones on the canvas if helpful.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">03</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">The Base Layer</h3>
            <p>Before the crowd arrives, establish the foundational elements. Paint the structural
            outlines, key features, and any elements that need artistic precision. This gives
            participants a framework to build upon.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">04</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">Facilitating the Crowd</h3>
            <p>This is where the magic happens. Guide participants to specific areas, suggest colors,
            and encourage bold strokes. The goal is controlled chaos — enough freedom for individual
            expression, enough structure for a cohesive result.</p>
            <div class="step__tip">
              <strong>Tip:</strong> Work in waves. Let 5-10 people paint at once, then rotate.
              Document every stage with photos — the process is as important as the product.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">05</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">The UV Layer</h3>
            <p>After the visible painting is complete, add the phosphorescent layer. This can be
            hidden symbols, glowing patterns, or entirely new imagery that only appears under
            blacklight. It's the painting's secret soul.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">06</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">The Reveal</h3>
            <p>Turn off the lights. Turn on the blacklight. Watch the room react. The hidden layer
            transforms everything — what was invisible becomes the centerpiece. It's a moment of
            collective wonder that makes the entire experience unforgettable.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="hiw-cta reveal">
        <h3 class="font-display hiw-cta__title">Ready to Try It Yourself?</h3>
        <p class="hiw-cta__desc">
          Download vector templates to get started, or commission a guided MetaPainting experience.
        </p>
        <div class="hiw-cta__actions">
          <a href="/templates" class="btn btn--primary">Get Templates</a>
          <a href="/commission" class="btn btn--outline">Commission a Painting</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .intro__text {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.5rem;
  }

  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .step__marker {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .step__number {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--color-teal);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .step__title {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .step__content p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 650px;
  }

  .step__tip {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-teal);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .step__tip strong {
    color: var(--color-teal);
  }

  .hiw-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 4rem 0 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }

  .hiw-cta__title {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .hiw-cta__desc {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .hiw-cta__actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .step {
      grid-template-columns: 40px 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
